<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Makaba II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1824">1824</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Makaba II was chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangwaketse">Bangwaketse</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tswana-people">Tswana people</a> of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>, in the late 18th and early 19th centuries. A successful raider and trader in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">furs</a>, he made the Bangwaketse one of the strongest Tswana states, and European travellers visited his large town. He was killed in 1824 during the upheavals of that period, when his people were attacked by migrating Kololo forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sebetwane">Sebetwane</a>.</p></div>
